Package: piprkitR
Title: R Interface to 'piprkit' for Pupil Light Response Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("S.", "Belgers", , "s.belgers@tue.nl", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An R interface to 'piprkit', a 'Python' package for processing
    pupil data with a focus on the post-illumination pupil response (PIPR):
    filtering, blink removal, baseline correction, PIPR metrics, and fitting
    a phase model of the pupil light response. The complete 'piprkit' API is
    available from R through 'reticulate'. All computations run in the
    'Python' package, so the results are identical to those in 'Python'.
    'Python' and 'piprkit' are installed automatically on first use.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/SBelgers/piprkitR,
    https://github.com/SBelgers/piprkit, https://sbelgers.github.io/piprkit/
BugReports: https://github.com/SBelgers/piprkitR/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.0)
Imports:
    graphics,
    reticulate (>= 1.41)
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.12) with the 'piprkit' package; both are
    installed automatically by 'reticulate' on first use.
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
